  "details": "This is an idea for the VRC Animator Play Audio feature that I’d like to propose. It may not be a strictly necessary feature, but for complex system customization, this might be essential.\n\nThis feature would allow the [Animator State] to end when the duration of the currently playing audio clip finishes. By using a calculated speed multiplier float from the Animator Play Audio State Behavior.\n\nNormally, I will manually do this by calculate the [Speed] value by taking 1 divided by the duration of the audio clip. This gives the proper speed for that state. For example, if the audio clip is 2.5 seconds long, then 1 / 2.5 equals 0.4. If you set the [Speed] to 0.4 while using a 1-second keyframe animation, this animation state will end exactly at the same time the audio finishes playing. (2.5 seconds : 0.4 animation speed)\n\nThe idea is to make VRC Animator Play Audio calculate a user-defined speed multiplier float (like Physbone prefix). Then user can use this calculated float in the [Multiplier] field to make any animation state speed end at the same time with the current playing audio.\n\nPlease refer to the attached image for better understanding.",
